                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I went into Monster Prom thinking it would be a cute little dating sim where I’d flirt with a vampire and call it a day. Instead I got a chaotic, hilarious, surprisingly deep game that has now consumed an unreasonable portion of my life. My roommate and I play this together, and I cannot recommend it enough as a shared experience. It is a veritable bonding experience, and honestly a better test of friendship than any group project I’ve ever survived. We have gone through the full mountain range of emotions together: joy, betrayal, secondhand embarrassment, and one deeply unexpected moment where we both got a little misty-eyed. Over a game about monsters going to prom. Let that sink in.\r\nWhat really gets us is the sheer amount of content. Every character has multiple routes, endings, secrets, and fun little surprises hiding around every corner, and just when you think you’ve seen it all, the game says “lol no” and hands you something new. My roommate and I are genuinely in awe of how much love the devs poured into this thing. You can feel it in every joke, every character quirk, every ridiculous ending. Someone out there cared deeply about making this game as fun and replayable as possible, and it shows.",
